# ${FEATURE_NAME}/

Feature folder for `${FEATURE_NAME}`. Stamped from the `_feature_template/`.

## What lives here

| Subfolder | What lives here | Naming suffix |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [`components/`](components/) | React components for this feature | `*.tsx` |
| [`hooks/`](hooks/) | React Query hooks + plain hooks | `use*.ts` |
| [`services/`](services/) | Network calls + business logic | `*.service.ts` |
| [`types/`](types/) | Request/response and domain types | `*.types.ts` |

## What does NOT live here

- Cross-feature UI primitives → `${SRC_DIR}/components/`.
- Shared hooks (used by 2+ features) → `${SRC_DIR}/hooks/`.
- Framework-agnostic helpers → `${SRC_DIR}/lib/`.
- Cross-feature types → `${SRC_DIR}/types/shared.ts`.

## Next steps

1. Rename this folder to your actual feature name (kebab-case, e.g. `users`, `orders`).
2. Replace the empty subfolders' `.gitkeep` files with real `*.tsx` / `use*.ts` / `*.service.ts` / `*.types.ts` files.
3. Mount the feature's page component in `${SRC_DIR}/routes/index.tsx`.
4. Add a test under `${SRC_DIR}/tests/unit/`.

